{"id":"cmr3rkc19005bjbhnpsgst2gj","description":"On On: Grandholm Garden, Bridge of Don.  Plenty of free parking on the cobbled street along the north bank of the River Don adjacent to Grandholm Garden.  \nApproaching from the south proceed via Gordon Mills Rd, Woodside, then turn right immediately after crossing over Grandholm Bridge. If coming from the north, enter the Grandholm estate off Gordon Brae, then park at the cobbled southern end of Grandholm Avenue beyond house no 8 near AB22 8AU\nWhat3Words: drips.smoke.occurs. \nGooglemaps link: \n\nhttps://goo.gl/maps/R1aSFijmDtX9KehM9","street":"Grandholm Gardens, AB22 8AG","loc":null,"cost":"£3","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rkc60005djbhngn0x0izz","description":"On On: East Woodlands, Pitmedden Road, Kirkhill, Dyce AB21 0HD\nMap ref: 57.220778, -2.241167 Googlemaps Ref:\n\nhttps://goo.gl/maps/nmQRtaQ75cmD3RDV7\nWhat3Words: deeper.activity.headsets - https://w3w.co/deeper.activity.headsets\n\nNB - Restricted parking so car share if possible.  On arrival drive round the house on the dirt track and follow indications to park on the sand school or nearby.\n\nDriving Directions - Coming from town head to the airport. Turn off A96 beyond the P&J Live on to Dyce Drive for the airport. At the lights by the airport entrance go straight ahead on Dyce Drive.  Coming from western regions via the peripheral road exit at A96 for the airport and head for the airport. At the lights turn left onto Dyce Drive. Coming from Bridge of Don side of town head to Dyce via B977 and then A947 then turn right on to Dyce Drive after crossing the River Don.\n\nFollow Dyce Drive through the industrial estate back into farmland and just before the bridge over the railway, turn left on Pitmedden Road signposted Dyce Churchyard and Kinaldie. Follow this road for 1.8 miles under the AWPR peripheral road bridge then bear left, do NOT turn right to Dyce Church yard. Go uphill through a series of bends past houses, after a small felled woodland by a cottage there will be a left hand turn on a right hand bend with signs for East Woodlands, take this up the narrow driveway and then left at the top and round the house to the parking.\n\nOn Inn: chez Tonto & Egg Foo for BBQ at East Woodlands of burgers, salad, veggie options, etc before the Circle","street":null,"loc":null,"cost":"£3","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
