{"id":"cmr3ruknb00031jhnceddvadn","description":"Next full moon is upon us, and time for another fun run in Leiden. Bring your flashlights/torches and come for some fun running! The beer is cold, and perhaps if spring turns back into winter, we will arrange warm drinks!\n\nThe start is in front of the Mercedes dealer behind the station. Less than 10min walk, and you'll see the car parked there somewhere.\n\nHare: Opee\nHash Cash: €5\nBag Drop: Yes!","street":null,"loc":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rukru00051jhnmoo693qy","description":"The full moon is upon us, and it's time to head back to The Hague. To mix things up, we even have a new hare--FILTH newcomer Boerskin. The intense rains and winds seem to be behind us, so grab your flashlights/torches and join us for some fun running! \n\nThe hare is kind enough to allow us to invade his home so we have somewhere to drop our bags and to warm up afterwards. There lots of free street parking in front of the house. Public transport: from Den Haag Centraal, take Tram 9 direction Scheveningen, get off at the Javabrug stop and then walk 300m.\n\nHare: Boerskin\nHash Cash: €5\nBag Drop: Yes!","street":"24A Bachmanstraat, 2596JC","loc":"Bachmanstraat 24, 2596 JC Den Haag, Nederland","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rukwy00071jhnfzdn18wd","description":"NOTE 1: We have 3 start times to allow people working in AMS ample time to get to the run and then enjoy the Beach festival with us!\n\nNOTE 2: Opee is offering crash space to anyone that wants to chill at the beach late and then return to AMS the next morning.\n\n=======\n\nDETAILS\n\nIt's hard to believe that one of the best places to chill is on the beach in front of a bonfire, but trust me, it's hard to find a place to be more relaxed.\n\nJoin me and other FILTH Hashers at this year's Bonfire Beach Festival at Scheveningen Beach. First runners off at 19:30, but there will be options to join the run at 20:00 and 20:30 as well. The end will be at the Bonfire Beach Festival where we will spend the next 3-4 hours hanging out on the beach, drinking wine and watching the long slow sunset.\n\nWe will have some beer for down-downs, but we plan to go to a local store immediately after the run so we can each purchase wine, cheese and other snacks for our chill to time on the beach.\n\nHope to see you there...  VIRGINS welcome! :-)\n\nOnOn! \nOpee\n\n========== Details ==========\n\nRun #: 146\nTheme: Bonfire Beach Festival\nDate: Friday, 19 Apr\nTime: 19:30\nLocation: Scheveningen Beach Pier (where the pier meets the boardwalk)\nBag Drop: Yes (and bring a beach blanket too!)\nHash cash: €5.00\nRSVP: Yes, please! On Facebook or send e-mail to [redacted]\n\nNOTE: If you want to join us later because you are unable to get to the beach by 19:30, no problem. You will be able to join the trail at 20:00 and 20:30 as well. We cater to all needs!","street":"Strandweg 152, 2586JW","loc":"DePier","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rul1u00091jhnip6a7n1r","description":"(NOTE: If you cannot make 10:30, but still want to join for brunch, see the note at the end of the post)\n\nAfter an intense few days partying in The Hague for King's Night and then partying with H4 in The Hague or in Amsterdam for King's Day, what better way to recover than to run with the FILTH Hash in Leiden!\n\nWe'll start at the Leiden train station (lockers are available) and make our way through the lovely Leiden canals on a short(ish) run that will end in a city park where we will have a champagne brunch complete with delicious baked goods, fruit, eggs and juices.\n\nFirst you'll party like a King, then Hash like a King and then you'll eat like a King!\n\nRSVP REQUIRED:  No RSVP, means you will be at the end of the food line and we won't be able to guarantee there will be enough. Please RSVP to: [redacted] or by SMS'ing [redacted].\n\nHope to see you there!\n\nOnOn!\n\nOpee\n\nNote: we are timing this run so that people from Brussels will have the opportunity to run, eat and get back to BXL for the BMPH3 AGM.\n\n==============\n\nDetails:\nRun number: n/a (this is a FILTH non-numbered event)\nDate: 28 Apr\nTime: 10:30 pack off\nLocation: Leiden Central Station, exit on the city side\nHares: Give it a Blow & Opee\nRun fee: €5 + €5 if you want brunch\nRSVP: Required if you want us to hold food for you\nBag drop: Yes, lockers are available at the station\n\nNOTE for latecomers: If you think you will be late, please let me know and I will connect you into the WhatsApp group we are setting up for the run. We will then allow you to live track the hares and join the trail in progress or meet us at the end.","street":"Stationsplein 3, 2312 AJ","loc":"Leiden Centraal railway station","cost":"€10","clear_run":147,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rul6b000b1jhn30fuyypc","description":"Let's get FILTHY with Patti!\n\nCome and celebrate Patti's 40th birthday in true Hash style... with lots of beer, partying (and maybe some other intoxicants).\n\nThe fun starts at the classic Genever bar, Wyland Fockink in Amsterdam. We will then do a running pub crawl to at least 3 other different venues. At any point, you can switch from the FILTH runner's trail to the walker's trail if you decide you've logged enough kilometers.\n\nBEWARE: There is NO bag drop. So please travel light! There will be walkers if you want to find someone to carry some small personal items for you.\n\nHope to see you all there!\n\nOnOn!\n\nOpee\n\n======= DETAILS =======\n\nRun #: FILTH #147\nDate: SATURDAY, May 18th\nTime: 19:00\nLocation: Wyland Fockink, Amsterdam\nRun fee: €5.00\nBag drop: NO... please carry what you bring or find a willing friend\nRSVP: Yes, to this FB event or to [redacted]\nTheme: Patti's 40th Birthday Bash!","street":"Pijlsteeg 31, 1012 HH","loc":"Wynand Fockink Tastingroom, Distillery & Liqueur store","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rulbb000d1jhnu4u56umj","description":"Meet next to the Mercedes Dealer 'behind' the station. Exit city side, walk right past all the bikes, past the first bridge, then turn right under the second bridge. You should see us on the left. Or user the map pin.\nHare: Tasty Piss\nBag Drop: Yes","street":"vondellaan 45, 2332 aa","loc":"Mercedes-Benz Leiden","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rulg7000f1jhn3w1010mm","description":"It is with great sadness that we will soon be bidding farewell to Strobe My Balls, who was named at the FILTH in 2016. He has embraced being a Dutch hasher all the way down to his wooden shoes. Don't miss your chance to hash on his last sh*tty FILTH trail. He promises a happy ending for all who make the trip out to Utrecht.\n\n======== Details ========\nTime: 19:30\nDate: Friday 19 July\nHare: Strobe My Balls\nLocation: Oudegracht 279, Utrecht\nA to A*\nBag drop: Yes\nHash cash: €5","street":"279 Oudegracht, 3511PA","loc":"Oudegracht 279","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rulkn000h1jhnmjr15q67","description":"Meet in the parking lot of \"De Stal\" opposite the Naturalis Museum. Very short walk from the station.\n\nHash Cash: €5\nHare: Tasty Piss\nBag Drop: Yes","street":"Darwinweg 1","loc":"De Stal","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruloy000j1jhnh9x66a6m","description":"A wonderful trail, followed by a BBQ in Overveen, and potentially swimming if the RA does a good job! :-)\n\nLocation: Overveen train station\nHare: Give it a Blow & Start Me Up\nBag Drop: Yes\nA-B run (bag drop will move)\nHash Cash: €10","street":"Tetterodeweg 2","loc":"Station Overveen","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rultu000l1jhnjjr8jd14","description":"The FILTH is celebrating Canadian HashGiving this year with The Hague H3 by starting at the same location that they will be having an earlier hash. You're welcome to come for one or both. See below for the separate registration for The Hague's special hash, which includes dinner for the early birds.  \n\n======== Details ========\nWhen: Sunday 13 October at 19:30\nHare: Do Me Moore + Joe Dirt\nLocation: Hoornbruglaan 47, 2281 AV Rijswijk, Nederland\nBag drop: Yes\nHash cash: €5\n\nThere will be a The Hague Hash run right before, at 14:00, so join both!\n\nRSVP: register for this event on The Hague H3 website:\nhttps://www.haguehash.nl/thanksgiving\nThe Moore Dirts are providing food for the first 30 people. More than 30 hashers are always welcome, but they will have to order pizza or something at their own expense. \n\nHares: Joe Dirt and Do Me Moore\nWhen: Sunday October 13th at 14:00 hrs\nWhere: Chez Moore Dirt, Hoornbruglaan 47, 2281 AV Rijswijk\nGood to know: Bring Your Own Drinks for Dinner\nHash cash: €5\n\nJoe Dirt and Do Me Moore are planning once again to host HashThanksGiving. However, this year they are traveling back stateside for actual American Thanksgiving. So they are haring HashGiving around Canadian ThanksGiving on Sunday 13 October (yes indeed, one whole day before the Canadian Thanksgiving and a whopping 46 days before the real one)\n\nThere will be the now traditional picture run at 14:00 with the meal to follow. The meal will be free for the first 30 people to fill out the form and commit to bringing your own drinks for dinner.\n\nThen at 19:30 there will be the October FILTH run at the same location. This means two hashes & two circles & two times hash cash (you are getting twice the beer).","street":"47 Hoornbruglaan, 2281AV","loc":"Hoornbruglaan 47, 2281 AV Rijswijk, Nederland","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rulz4000n1jhn7a8uhdk0","description":"World leaders don't seem to be making much progress with diplomacy... there HAS to be a better way. Well, we think there is and it's BEER. Join us at the Hague Humanity Hub in The Hague where we will explore what it means to make Peace with bottles in our hands.\n\nHope to see you all there! Bring friends and virgins so we can have even more peace!\n\n====== Details ======\n\nRun #: n/a\nTheme: World Piece Through Beer\nDate: Thur 24 Oct\nTime: 19:00 gather / 19:15 pack off\nBag Drop: Yes\nRun Fee: €5.00","street":"58 Fluwelen Burgwal, 2511CJ","loc":"Fluwelen Burgwal 58, 2511 CJ Den Haag, Nederland","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rum41000p1jhnpj7kguot","description":"FILTH 154 will be on Monday 11 November! Double time to celebrate, as it's the start of carnival, and we will celebrate South Africa's World Cup victory. So either dress up as something worthy of carnival, or wear green and gold, OR BOTH!\n\nHash Cash: €5\nBag Drop: Yes, the Pub\nHare: Boar Whore","street":"oude singel 2, 2312RA","loc":"Duke of Oz","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rum8e000r1jhnkl0dvpy3","description":"Whilst the UK is taken over by Election Fever and School Nativity Plays are being disrupted, we'll have a hash under the light of the December Cold Full Moon. First results could be coming in as circle is drawing to a close.. Spannend!\n\nLocation : Chez Edge\nDag Drop : Yes\nHash Cash : 5 euro or £5\nHare : On The Edge","street":null,"loc":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
